# IC-7610 CI-V command catalog extracted from IC-7610_ENG_CI-V_0a.pdf (A7380-7EX). Format CMD|SUB|DATA|NAME|NOTES
# Default address 98h, controller E0h. Frame FE FE <to> <from> Cn [Sc] [data] FD ; OK=FB, NG=FA. Asterisk (*) in manual = send/read data. No 29 receiver-prefix on this model (uses 07 D0/D1 main/sub select and cmd 25/26).
# Footnotes: *1 ANT1/ANT2 RX ANT ON invalid if antenna type is RX-I/O (00 always returned); *2 53 ON invalid if type RX-ANT; *3 CW msg sent only in CW mode with TX/break-in; *4 power ON (18 01) needs repeated FE preamble (4800:7, 9600:13, 19200:25, 38400:50, 57600:75, 115200:150); *5 read only; *6 memory keyer counter; *7 USB[1] needs CI-V USB Port=Unlink from REMOTE and CI-V Baud=115200 (LAN port always ok)
# FREQ = BCD 5 bytes LSB first: [10Hz 1Hz][1kHz 100Hz][100kHz 10kHz][10MHz 1MHz][1GHz 100MHz]
00||FREQ BCD 5 bytes (see p.10)|Send frequency data (transceive)|
01||MODE 2 bytes: mode,filter (see p.10)|Send mode data (transceive)|mode 00 LSB,01 USB,02 AM,03 CW,04 RTTY,05 FM,07 CW-R,08 RTTY-R,12 PSK,13 PSK-R; filter 01 FIL1,02 FIL2,03 FIL3 (filter byte may be skipped: FIL1 for 01)
02||BAND EDGE (see p.10): edge no. + lower 5B BCD + 2D + upper 5B BCD|Read band edge frequencies|edge number not returned when obtaining with 02
03||FREQ BCD 5 bytes|Read operating frequency|
04||MODE 2 bytes: mode,filter|Read operating mode|
05||FREQ BCD 5 bytes|Set operating frequency|
06||MODE 1-2 bytes: mode[,filter]|Set operating mode|filter may be skipped: default filter of the mode is selected
07||(none)|Select the VFO mode|
07|B0||Exchange main and sub bands|
07|B1||Equalize main and sub bands|
07|C0||Turn OFF Dualwatch|
07|C1||Turn ON Dualwatch|
07|C2|00 or 01|Send/read the dualwatch setting|00=OFF 01=ON; send/read (*)
07|D0||Select the main band|
07|D1||Select the sub band|
07|D2|00 or 01|Send/read main/sub band selection|00=main band selection 01=sub band selection; send/read (*)
08||(none)|Select the Memory mode|
08||BCD 2 bytes 0001 to 0099|Select the Memory channel|0001=M-CH01, 0099=M-CH99
08||BCD 2 bytes 0100|Select program scan edge channel P1|
08||BCD 2 bytes 0101|Select program scan edge channel P2|
09||(none)|Memory write|
0A||(none)|Memory copy to VFO|
0B||(none)|Memory clear|
0E|00||Cancel the scan|
0E|01||Start a Programmed/memory scan|
0E|02||Start a Programmed scan|
0E|03||Start a F scan|
0E|12||Start a Fine programmed scan|
0E|13||Start a Fine F scan|
0E|22||Start a Memory scan|
0E|23||Start a Select memory scan|
0E|A1~A7||Select F scan span|x=1..7: A1 +-5 kHz, A2 +-10 kHz, A3 +-20 kHz, A4 +-50 kHz, A5 +-100 kHz, A6 +-500 kHz, A7 +-1 MHz
0E|B0||Clear the Select channel setting|
0E|B1||Set as select channel|previously set number by CI-V is set after power ON, or 1 if none selected
0E|B1|01 to 03|Set the channel as a Select channel|01=SEL1 02=SEL2 03=SEL3
0E|B2|00 to 03|Set the Select memory scan channel|00=ALL 01=SEL1 02=SEL2 03=SEL3
0E|D0||Set Scan resume OFF|
0E|D3||Set Scan resume ON|
0F||(none) request|Read Split setting|manual rows 'Read Split OFF setting'=00 / 'Read Split ON setting'=01 (reply value)
0F|00||Turn OFF the Split function|
0F|01||Turn ON the Split function|
10||00 to 08|Send/read the tuning step|send/read (*); 00=OFF (10 Hz or 1 Hz),01=100 Hz,02=1 kHz,03=5 kHz,04=9 kHz,05=10 kHz,06=12.5 kHz,07=20 kHz,08=25 kHz
11||BCD 1 byte 00,03,06,09,12,15,18,21,24,27,30,33,36,39,42,45|Send/read attenuator|send/read (*); value = attenuation in dB, 00=OFF
12|00|00 or 01|Select/read ANT1 selection|send/read (*); 00=RX ANT OFF 01=RX ANT ON; footnote *1
12|01|00 or 01|Select/read ANT2 selection|send/read (*); 00=RX ANT OFF 01=RX ANT ON; footnote *1
13|00||Speech all data with voice synthesizer|S meter level, frequency and mode
13|01||Speech operating frequency and S meter level|
13|02||Speech operating mode|mode announced after ongoing speech
14|01|BCD 2 bytes 0000~0255|Send/read AF level|send/read (*); 0000=min 0255=max
14|02|BCD 2 bytes 0000~0255|Send/read RF gain|0000=min 0255=max
14|03|BCD 2 bytes 0000~0255|Send/read squelch level|0000=min 0255=max
14|05|BCD 2 bytes 0000~0255|Send/read APF level|10 Hz steps; 0000=Pitch-550 Hz 0128=Pitch 0255=Pitch+550 Hz
14|06|BCD 2 bytes 0000~0255|Send/read NR level|0000=0% 0255=100%
14|07|BCD 2 bytes 0000~0255|Send/read inner TWIN PBT position|0000=max CCW 0128=center 0255=max CW
14|08|BCD 2 bytes 0000~0255|Send/read outer TWIN PBT position|0000=max CCW 0128=center 0255=max CW
14|09|BCD 2 bytes 0000~0255|Send/read CW pitch|5 Hz steps; 0000=300 Hz 0128=600 Hz 0255=900 Hz
14|0A|BCD 2 bytes 0000~0255|Send/read RF power|0000=min 0255=max
14|0B|BCD 2 bytes 0000~0255|Send/read MIC gain|0000=min 0255=max
14|0C|BCD 2 bytes 0000~0255|Send/read keying speed|0000=6 wpm 0255=48 wpm
14|0D|BCD 2 bytes 0000~0255|Send/read Notch filter setting|0000=max CCW 0128=center 0255=max CW
14|0E|BCD 2 bytes 0000~0255|Send/read COMP level|0000=0 0255=10
14|0F|BCD 2 bytes 0000~0255|Send/read Break-IN delay|0000=2.0 d 0255=13.0 d
14|12|BCD 2 bytes 0000~0255|Send/read NB level|0000=0% 0255=100%
14|13|BCD 2 bytes 0000~0255|Send/read DIGI-SEL shift amount|0000=min 0255=max
14|14|BCD 2 bytes 0000~0255|Send/read DRIVE gain|0000=0% 0255=100%
14|15|BCD 2 bytes 0000~0255|Send/read Monitor audio [MONI] level|0000=0% 0255=100%
14|16|BCD 2 bytes 0000~0255|Send/read VOX gain|0000=0% 0255=100%
14|17|BCD 2 bytes 0000~0255|Send/read Anti VOX gain|0000=0% 0255=100%
14|19|BCD 2 bytes 0000~0255|Send/read LCD backlight brightness|0000=0% 0255=100%
15|01|00 or 01|Read noise or S-meter squelch status|00=Close 01=Open; read only
15|02|BCD 2 bytes 0000 to 0255|Read S-meter level|0000=S0 0120=S9 0241=S9+60 dB
15|05|00 or 01|Read various squelch (tone squelch etc) status|00=Close 01=Open
15|07|00 or 01|Read the Overflow status|00=OVF indicator OFF 01=ON
15|11|BCD 2 bytes 0000~0255|Read PO meter level|0000=0% 0143=50% 0212=100%
15|12|BCD 2 bytes 0000~0255|Read SWR meter level|0000=SWR1.0 0048=1.5 0080=2.0 0120=3.0
15|13|BCD 2 bytes 0000~0255|Read ALC meter level|0000=min 0120=max
15|14|BCD 2 bytes 0000~0255|Read COMP meter level|0000=0 dB 0130=15 dB 0241=30 dB
15|15|BCD 2 bytes 0000~0255|Read Vd meter level|0000=0 V 0151=10 V 0211=16 V
15|16|BCD 2 bytes 0000~0255|Read Id meter level|0000=0A 0077=10A 0165=20A 0241=30A
16|02|00,01,02|Preamp|send/read (*); 00=Preamp OFF 01=Preamp 1 ON 02=Preamp 2 ON
16|12|01 ~ 03|Set the AGC time constant|01=FAST 02=MID 03=SLOW
16|22|00 or 01|Set the Noise blanker|00=OFF 01=ON
16|32|00,01,02,03|Audio peak filter|00=OFF 01=WIDE ON (320 Hz if SHARP APF) 02=MID ON (160 Hz) 03=NAR ON (80 Hz)
16|40|00 or 01|Set the Noise reduction|00=OFF 01=ON
16|41|00 or 01|Set the Auto Notch function|00=OFF 01=ON
16|42|00 or 01|Set the Repeater tone|00=OFF 01=ON
16|43|00 or 01|Set the Tone squelch|00=OFF 01=ON
16|44|00 or 01|Set the Speech compressor|00=OFF 01=ON
16|45|00 or 01|Set the Monitor [MONI] function|00=OFF 01=ON
16|46|00 or 01|Set the VOX function|00=OFF 01=ON
16|47|00,01,02|BK-IN function|00=OFF 01=Semi BK-IN ON 02=Full BK-IN ON
16|48|00 or 01|Set the Manual Notch function|00=OFF 01=ON
16|4E|00 or 01|Set the DIGI-SEL function|00=OFF 01=ON
16|4F|00 or 01|Set the Twin peak filter|00=OFF 01=ON; ON only when RTTY Mark=2125 Hz and Shift=170 Hz
16|50|00 or 01|Set the Dial lock function|00=OFF 01=ON
16|53|00 or 01|Set the ANT-RX I/O|00=OFF 01=ON; footnote *2
16|56|00 or 01|Set the DSP IF filter type|00=SHARP 01=SOFT
16|57|00 ~ 02|Set the Manual Notch width|00=WIDE 01=MID 02=NAR
16|58|00 ~ 02|Set the SSB transmit bandwidth|00=WIDE 01=MID 02=NAR; applied value depends on COMP ON/OFF: WIDE=1A 05 0015, MID=1A 05 0016, NAR=1A 05 0017
16|5E|00 or 01|MAIN/SUB Tracking function|00=OFF 01=ON
16|65|00 or 01|Set the IP Plus function|00=OFF 01=ON
17||ASCII text up to 30 chars (see p.10)|Send CW messages|footnote *3; FF stops sending; ^ = no inter-character space
18|00||Turn OFF the transceiver|
18|01||Turn ON the transceiver|footnote *4 (preceding FE bytes needed)
19|00||Read the transceiver ID|
1A|00|see p.11|Send/read memory contents|send/read (*)
1A|01|see p.10|Send/read band stacking register contents|send/read (*)
1A|02|see p.13|Send/read memory keyer contents|send/read (*); footnote *6
1A|03|see p.12|Send/read the selected IF filter width|send/read (*)
1A|04|see p.12|Send/read the selected AGC time constant|send/read (*)
1A|05 00 01|see p. 12|Tone Control > RX > Send/read SSB RX HPF/LPF settings|
1A|05 00 02|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|Tone Control > RX > Send/read SSB RX Tone (Bass) level|(00=-5 to 10=+5)
1A|05 00 03|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|Tone Control > RX > Send/read SSB RX Tone (Treble) level|(00=-5 to 10=+5)
1A|05 00 04|see p. 12|Tone Control > RX > Send/read AM RX HPF/LPF settings|
1A|05 00 05|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|Tone Control > RX > Send/read AM RX Tone (Bass) level|(00=-5 to 10=+5)
1A|05 00 06|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|Tone Control > RX > Send/read AM RX Tone (Treble) level|(00=-5 to 10=+5)
1A|05 00 07|see p. 12|Tone Control > RX > Send/read FM RX HPF/LPF settings|
1A|05 00 08|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|Tone Control > RX > Send/read FM RX Tone (Bass) level|(00=-5 to 10=+5)
1A|05 00 09|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|Tone Control > RX > Send/read FM RX Tone (Treble) level|(00=-5 to 10=+5)
1A|05 00 10|see p. 12|Tone Control > RX > Send/read CW RX HPF/LPF settings|
1A|05 00 11|see p. 12|Tone Control > RX > Send/read RTTY RX HPF/LPF settings|
1A|05 00 12|see p. 12|Tone Control > RX > Send/read PSK RX HPF/LPF settings|
1A|05 00 13|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|Tone Control > TX > Send/read SSB TX Tone (Bass) level|(00=-5 to 10=+5)
1A|05 00 14|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|Tone Control > TX > Send/read SSB TX Tone (Treble) level|(00=-5 to 10=+5)
1A|05 00 15|see p. 12|Tone Control > TX > Send/read SSB TX bandwidth for wide|
1A|05 00 16|see p. 12|Tone Control > TX > Send/read SSB TX bandwidth for mid|
1A|05 00 17|see p. 12|Tone Control > TX > Send/read SSB TX bandwidth for narrow|
1A|05 00 18|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|Tone Control > TX > Send/read AM TX Tone (Bass) level|(00=-5 to 10=+5)
1A|05 00 19|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|Tone Control > TX > Send/read AM TX Tone (Treble) level|(00=-5 to 10=+5)
1A|05 00 20|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|Tone Control > TX > Send/read FM TX Tone (Bass) level|(00=-5 to 10=+5)
1A|05 00 21|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|Tone Control > TX > Send/read FM TX Tone (Treble) level|(00=-5 to 10=+5)
1A|05 00 22|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Function > Beep Level|(0000=min. to 0255=max.)
1A|05 00 23|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Function > Beep Level Limit|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 24|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Function > Beep (Confirmation)|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 25|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Function > Band Edge Beep|(00=OFF, 01=ON) ( ON = Beep sounds with a default amateur band) 02 Function > Band Edge Beep (02=ON (User)) 03 Function > Band Edge Beep (03=ON (User) & TX Limit) Cmd. Sub cmd. Data Description
1A|05 00 26|BCD 2 bytes 0050 ~ 0200|Function > Beep Sound (MAIN)|(0050=500 Hz to 0200=2000 Hz)
1A|05 00 27|BCD 2 bytes 0050 ~ 0200|Function > Beep Sound (SUB)|(0050=500 Hz to 0200=2000 Hz)
1A|05 00 28|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 02|Function > RF/SQL Control|(00=Auto, 01=SQL, 02=RF+SQL)
1A|05 00 29|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 05|Function > TX Delay > HF|(00=OFF, 01=10 ms, 02=15 ms, 03=20 ms, 04=25 ms, 05=30 ms)
1A|05 00 30|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 05|Function > TX Delay > 50M|(00=OFF, 01=10 ms, 02=15 ms, 03=20 ms, 04=25 ms, 05=30 ms)
1A|05 00 31|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 05|Function > Time-Out Timer (CI-V)|( 00=OFF, 01=3 min., 02=5 min., 03=10 min., 04=20 min., 05=30 min.)
1A|05 00 32|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Function > Quick Dualwatch|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 33|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Function > SPLIT > Quick SPLIT|(00=OFF, 01=ON) ( Setting the [SPLIT] key operation when it is held down for 1 second.)
1A|05 00 34|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Function > SPLIT > Display Keypad on Quick SPLIT|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 35|see p. 12|Function > SPLIT > FM SPLIT Offset (HF)|
1A|05 00 36|see p. 12|Function > SPLIT > FM SPLIT Offset (50M)|
1A|05 00 37|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Function > SPLIT > SPLIT LOCK|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 38|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Function > Tuner > PTT Start|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 39|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Function > Transverter Function|(00=Auto, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 40|see p. 12|Function > Transverter Offset|
1A|05 00 41|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 02|Function > RTTY Mark Frequency|(00=1275 Hz, 01=1615 Hz, 02=2125 Hz)
1A|05 00 42|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 02|Function > RTTY Shift Width|(00=170 Hz, 01=200 Hz, 02=425 Hz)
1A|05 00 43|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Function > RTTY Keying Polarity|(00=Normal, 01=Reverse)
1A|05 00 44|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 02|Function > PSK Tone Frequency|(00=1000 Hz, 01=1500 Hz, 02=2000 Hz)
1A|05 00 45|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Function > SPEECH > SPEECH Language|(00=English, 01=Japanese)
1A|05 00 46|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Function > SPEECH > SPEECH Speed|(00=Slow, 01=Fast)
1A|05 00 47|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Function > SPEECH > S-Level SPEECH|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 48|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Function > SPEECH > MODE SPEECH|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 49|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Function > SPEECH > SPEECH Level|(0000=0% to 0255=100%)
1A|05 00 50|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Function > [SPEECH/LOCK] Switch|(00=SPEECH/LOCK, 01=LOCK/SPEECH)
1A|05 00 51|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Function > Lock Function|(00=MAIN DIAL, 01=PANEL)
1A|05 00 52|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Function > Memo Pad Quantity|(00=5 ch, 01=10 ch)
1A|05 00 53|BCD 1 byte 00 to 02|Function > MAIN DIAL Auto TS|(00=OFF, 01=Low, 02=High)
1A|05 00 54|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Function > MAIN DIAL Select (USB DIAL-SUB Only)|(00=Main only, 01=Main/Sub)
1A|05 00 55|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Function > MAIN/SUB Tracking [MAIN/SUB] Switch|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 56|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Function > MIC Up/Down Speed|(00=Slow, 01=Fast)
1A|05 00 57|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Function > Quick RIT/TX Clear|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 58|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 02|Function > [NOTCH] Switch (SSB)|(00=Auto, 01=Manual, 02=Auto/Manual)
1A|05 00 59|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 02|Function > [NOTCH] Switch (AM)|(00=Auto, 01=Manual, 02=Auto/Manual)
1A|05 00 60|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Function > FILTER Screen MAIN/SUB Select|( 00=Fix, 01=Auto (by FILTER, PBT Operation))
1A|05 00 61|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Function > SSB/CW Synchronous Tuning|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 62|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Function > CW Normal Side|(00=LSB, 01=USB)
1A|05 00 63|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Function > Screen Keyboard Type|(00=Ten-key, 01=Full Keyboard)
1A|05 00 64|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 02|Function > Screen Full Keyboard Layout|(00=English, 01=German, 02=French)
1A|05 00 65|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Function > Screen Capture [POWER] Switch|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 66|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Function > Screen Capture Keyboard [Print Screen]|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 67|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Function > Screen Capture Storage Media|(00=SD Card, 01=USB flash drive)
1A|05 00 68|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Function > Screen Capture File Type|(00=PNG, 01=BMP)
1A|05 00 69|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Function > Calibration Marker|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 70|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0511|Function > REF Adjust|(0000=0%, 0511=100%)
1A|05 00 71|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 30|Connectors > Phones > Level|(00=-15 dB to 30=+15 dB)
1A|05 00 72|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Connectors > Phones > L/R Mix|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 73|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Connectors > ACC AF/IF Output > AF/SQL Output Select|(00=MAIN, 01=SUB)
1A|05 00 74|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Connectors > ACC AF/IF Output > Output Select|(00=AF, 01=IF)
1A|05 00 75|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Connectors > ACC AF/IF Output > AF/IF XFC Output (SPLIT ON)|(00=MAIN, 01=SUB)
1A|05 00 76|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Connectors > ACC AF/IF Output > AF Output Level|(0000=0% to 0255=100%)
1A|05 00 77|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Connectors > ACC AF/IF Output > AF SQL|(00=OFF (Open), 01=ON)
1A|05 00 78|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Connectors > ACC AF/IF Output > AF Beep/Speech... Output|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 79|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Connectors > ACC AF/IF Output > ACC IF Output Level|(0000=0% to 0255=100%)
1A|05 00 80|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Connectors > USB AF/IF Output > Output Select|(00=AF, 01=IF)
1A|05 00 81|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Connectors > USB AF/IF Output > AF/IF XFC Output (SPLIT ON)|(00=MAIN, 01=SUB)
1A|05 00 82|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Connectors > USB AF/IF Output > AF Output Level|(0000=0%, 0255=100%)
1A|05 00 83|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Connectors > USB AF/IF Output > AF SQL|(00=OFF (Open), 01=ON)
1A|05 00 84|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Connectors > USB AF/IF Output > AF Beep/Speech... Output|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 85|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Connectors > USB AF/IF Output > IF Output Level|(0000=0%, 0255=100%)
1A|05 00 86|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Connectors > LAN AF/IF Output > Output Select|(00=AF, 01=IF)
1A|05 00 87|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Connectors > LAN AF/IF Output > AF SQL|(00=OFF (Open), 01=ON)
1A|05 00 88|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Connectors > MOD Input > ACC MOD Level|(0000=0% to 0255=100%)
1A|05 00 89|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Connectors > MOD Input > USB MOD Level|(0000=0% to 0255=100%)
1A|05 00 90|BCD 2 bytes 0000 ~ 0255|Connectors > MOD Input > LAN MOD Level|(0000=0% to 0255=100%)
1A|05 00 91|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 05|Connectors > MOD Input > DATA OFF MOD|( 00=MIC, 01=ACC, 02=MIC,ACC, 03=USB, 04=MIC,USB, 05=LAN) Cmd. Sub cmd. Data Description
1A|05 00 92|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 05|Connectors > MOD Input > DATA1 MOD|( 00=MIC, 01=ACC, 02=MIC,ACC, 03=USB, 04=MIC,USB, 05=LAN)
1A|05 00 93|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 05|Connectors > MOD Input > DATA2 MOD|( 00=MIC, 01=ACC, 02=MIC,ACC, 03=USB, 04=MIC,USB, 05=LAN)
1A|05 00 94|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 05|Connectors > MOD Input > DATA3 MOD|( 00=MIC, 01=ACC, 02=MIC,ACC, 03=USB, 04=MIC,USB, 05=LAN)
1A|05 00 95|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 04|Connectors > USB SEND/Keying > USB SEND|( 00=OFF, 01=USB1(A) DTR, 02=USB1(A) RTS, 03=USB1(B) DTR, 04=USB1(B) RTS) ( You cannot select the same setting for USB keying (CW) or USB keying (RTTY).)
1A|05 00 96|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 04|Connectors > USB SEND/Keying > USB Keying (CW)|( 00=OFF, 01=USB1(A) DTR, 02=USB1(A) RTS, 03=USB1(B) DTR, 04=USB1(B) RTS) ( You cannot select the same setting for USB SEND.)
1A|05 00 97|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 04|Connectors > USB SEND/Keying > USB Keying (RTTY)|( 00=OFF, 01=USB1(A) DTR, 02=USB1(A) RTS, 03=USB1(B) DTR, 04=USB1(B) RTS) ( You cannot select the same setting for USB SEND.)
1A|05 00 98|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Connectors > External Keypad > VOICE|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 00 99|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Connectors > External Keypad > KEYER|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 01 00|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Connectors > External Keypad > RTTY|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 01 01|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Connectors > External Keypad > PSK|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 01 02|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Connectors > Keyboard/Mouse > Keyboard [F1] ~ [F8] (VOICE)|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 01 03|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Connectors > Keyboard/Mouse > Keyboard [F1] ~ [F8] (KEYER)|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 01 04|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 10|Connectors > Keyboard/Mouse > Keyboard Type|(00=English, 01=Japanese, 02=United Kingdom, 03=French, 04=French ( Canadian), 05=German, 06=Portuguese, 07=Portuguese (Brazilian), 08=Spanish, 09=Spanish (Latin American), 10=Italian)
1A|05 01 05|BCD 2 bytes 0010 ~ 0100|Connectors > Keyboard/Mouse > Keyboard Repeat Delay|( 0010=100 msec., 0100=1000 msec. (in 50 msec. steps))
1A|05 01 06|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 31|Connectors > Keyboard/Mouse > Keyboard Repeat Rate|(00=2.0 cps to 31=30.0 cps)
1A|05 01 07|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 02|Connectors > Keyboard/Mouse > Mouse Pointer Speed|(00=Slow, 01=Mid, 02=Fast)
1A|05 01 08|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Connectors > Keyboard/Mouse > Mouse Pointer Acceleration|(00=OFF, 01=ON)
1A|05 01 09|BCD 1 byte 00 or 01|Connectors > USB DIAL > USB DIAL Select|(00=Sub only, 01=Main/Sub)
1A|05 01 10|BCD 1 byte 00 ~ 02|Connectors > USB DIAL > USB DIAL Auto TS|(00=OFF, 01=Low, 02=High)
